td-sh conformance spec corpus
=============================

This directory holds the Oils-format spec-test cases the `td-sh` conformance
gate runs (see ../tests/conformance.rs). Two provenances live here:

Vendored from Oils (oils-for-unix/oils), UNMODIFIED
---------------------------------------------------
  Upstream:  https://github.com/oils-for-unix/oils
  Commit:    15de8fd779569e6e3a9f5fcbfc00e7df0ebe0380
  Path:      spec/<file>  (copied byte-for-byte)
  License:   Apache-2.0 (Oils). Copyright the Oils contributors.

  Selection rule (reproducible from the pin): every `spec/*.test.sh` at that
  commit EXCEPT
    - the YSH/Oil *language* files (`ysh-*`, `oil-*`, `hay*`, `func-parsing`,
      `proc-*`) — they test a different language, not a POSIX /bin/sh, so their
      cases can never go green here; and
    - Oils `smoke.test.sh`, whose name collides with td-sh's own seed below.
  That is the POSIX/bash-family shell-conformance set: 137 files.

  These files are pristine — the upstream bytes, verified byte-identical to that
  pinned commit (each file's git blob SHA matches the pin). td-sh's own view of
  which cases it cannot yet pass lives in `expectations.txt`, NOT as edits to
  these files, so a pin bump is a clean re-copy. `td_sh::parse_spec` reads the
  native Oils format directly (no conversion step). Bumping the pin, or changing
  the selection, is a reviewed change: re-copy, re-verify the blob SHAs, and
  regenerate `expectations.txt`.

td-sh-authored seed cases
-------------------------
  smoke.test.sh
  expansion.test.sh

  Hand-written in the same Oils format; the original RED-baseline seed corpus.
  Retained as additional, always-green coverage.

Overlay
-------
  expectations.txt   td-sh's known-gap manifest (xfail / skip). Not a spec file.
                     GENERATED, not hand-edited: examples/gen_expectations.rs runs
                     each case through the built td-sh and buckets it. See its
                     header for the xfail/skip semantics. Regenerate on a pin bump
                     or when passes change (do not hand-edit):

                       cargo build --release --manifest-path td-sh/Cargo.toml
                       cargo run --release --manifest-path td-sh/Cargo.toml \
                         --example gen_expectations -- \
                         target/release/td-sh td-sh/spec > td-sh/spec/expectations.txt
